WEBVTT

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:17.950
We're here.

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:26.910
This is my grandma's house.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.510
Yumi-chin, I'm back.

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:35.880
Welcome back.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.260
We're back!

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:40.260
Hey, Momo!

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:40.260
Senpai...

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:43.030
There's so much room!

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:44.130
Who are those people?

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:47.020
These are the girls I told you about, 
from Achiga Girls' Academy.

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:48.600
I'm from Tsuruga Academy.

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:52.030
Tsuruga Academy (Nagano)
3rd Year
Kajiki Yumi

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:50.040
My name's Kajiki Yumi.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:51.290
It's nice to meet you.

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:25.340
I see.

00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:30.210
You want to get stronger by tomorrow.

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:33.340
Please help us.

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:37.950
<b>Round 8:
Training</b>

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:38.340
We do have two top-ranked 
players in district,

00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:41.560
but since we placed third in our prefecture, 
we'd normally be lower than you.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:43.860
Also, I think you can't

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:46.600
expect a radical change in one day.

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:50.840
We know that as well, 
but as we are right now...

00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:59.240
Fine then.

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:01.700
Why don't we start out with a game?

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:04.330
Playing against Nara's top school will be

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:06.650
perfect for our younger players' growth.

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:09.080
Will one of you be playing in the individuals?

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:10.430
Um, no...

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:11.670
Yumi-chin!

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:12.580
Yeah.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:14.940
I'll go get her then!

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:16.030
Thanks.

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:19.640
Let's prepare the table in the meantime.

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:21.180
Okay.

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:22.360
Um.

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:23.800
Tournament rules say that

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:26.120
individual tournament players 
are not allowed to play

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:28.120
practice matches with any players

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:30.800
outside of their own school,

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:35.070
but since none of you have entered,

00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:36.220
it's not a problem.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:39.530
Then the person she went to get is...

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:40.510
Yes.

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:42.300
She's Nagano's number 
one individual player

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:43.950
and captain of Kazekoshi 
Girls' High School:

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:50.510
Fukuji Mihoko.

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:56.460
Captain Fukuji-san of Nagano's 
prestigious Kazekoshi Girls'...

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:57.530
Night snack.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:01.230
I made some.

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:01.800
Here it is.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:04.650
First ranked and considerate!

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:13.140
Achiga Girls' Academy
 Nara - 1st

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:16.610
Tsuruga Academy
 Nagano - 3rd

00:04:16.710 --> 00:04:20.150
Fukuji Mihoko
 Nagano Individuals - 1st

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:21.400
Let's begin.

00:04:30.810 --> 00:04:31.830
<i>Good.</i>

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:33.870
<i>The dora are coming my way today.</i>

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:42.020
<i>I've got so many warm tiles.</i>

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:47.420
<i>So these are the Matsumi sisters from 
Nara's representative school, Achiga...</i>

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.420
<i>Their specialties were reflected</i>

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:52.520
<i>quite strongly in the prefectural 
preliminary records...</i>

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:57.600
<i>Especially the younger 
sister, Matsumi Kuro.</i>

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:00.670
<i>Her specialty is really easy to spot.</i>

00:05:00.670 --> 00:05:04.110
<i>If those discard patterns aren't a 
product of coincidence, then...</i>

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:17.390
<i>Discard the red 5 of characters 
and she'll be in tenpai.</i>

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:19.880
<i>But I bet she will...</i>

00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:24.470
Ron.

00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:26.380
1,300.

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:30.160
<i>A kanchan wait.</i>

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:30.160
[kanchan - waiting for the middle tile in a sequence]

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:33.270
<i>She discarded the 6 of bamboo in the 
same turn and destroyed her three-sided wait!</i>

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:34.970
Could that possibly be...

00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:37.580
Sorry to disappoint,

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:41.730
but I don't have a weird power
 like Onjouji from Senriyama.

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:44.330
But Kuro-chan's...

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:47.870
I've been interested in the play records

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:49.530
for you two for a while now.

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:52.530
I thought about how I 
would play against you,

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:55.540
and this was one of my strategies.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:58.540
Does that answer your questions?

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:00.710
Yes!

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:04.880
Then let's continue.

00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:05.990
Second Match
South Hand 2

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:14.810
Riichi!

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:18.020
<i>She called that riichi 
really early, again.</i>

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:20.520
<i>It's scary how often she 
completes her hand.</i>

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:29.880
Ron.

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:37.170
She's called riichi, too?

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:40.350
<i>I get it...</i>

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:43.530
<i>This is what they mean by "disappear."</i>

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:45.070
Third Match
South Hand 1

00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:51.580
<i>All right, tenpai.</i>

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:53.930
<i>I can discard the 3 of circles and 
call riichi for guaranteed mangan.</i>

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:55.270
<i>If I tsumo and get some uradoras,</i>

00:06:55.270 --> 00:06:56.960
<i>this could even be a dealer baiman.</i>

00:06:56.960 --> 00:06:58.270
<i>Time to attack.</i>

00:06:58.270 --> 00:06:59.270
Riichi!

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:01.170
<i>A dealer riichi.</i>

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:04.020
<i>It looks like an expensive hand, too.</i>

00:07:05.470 --> 00:07:06.690
<i>Discard the 8 of bamboo and</i>

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:09.280
<i>switch to a two-way wait on 
the three and six instead...</i>

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:12.720
<i>The Achiga girls are doing</i>

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:15.990
<i>everything they can to get better.</i>

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:18.660
<i>Then all I can do is to answer</i>

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:21.330
<i>their feelings with everything I've got.</i>

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:30.650
<i>Looking at all the discards, 
it's probably a two-way wait</i>

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:32.680
<i>on the five and eight of bamboo.</i>

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:33.840
<i>In that case...</i>

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:42.270
<i>There goes my ippatsu.</i>

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:51.150
Riichi!

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:52.400
<i>She caught up to me.</i>

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:01.960
Tsumo.

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:03.420
4,000. 8,000.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:06.470
<i>She used up all the tiles 
I was waiting for!</i>

00:08:06.470 --> 00:08:10.320
<i>It's like she could see 
right through my hand.</i>

00:08:12.070 --> 00:08:16.390
Um, please play me next!

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:18.220
Of course.

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:19.890
I'll join, too.

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:22.140
I want to play again, too.

00:08:22.510 --> 00:08:24.020
Me too, please!

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:25.060
Me, too!

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:25.770
And me!

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:29.020
All right, I'll take you all on!

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:31.030
Come at me, all of you!

00:08:31.090 --> 00:08:32.740
Fourth Match

00:08:31.090 --> 00:08:32.740
East Hand 1

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:35.970
[iipeikou - double sequence in the same suit, e.g. 2-3-4/2-3-4]

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:35.970
Riichi, ippatsu, tsumo, tanyao, 
iipeikou, with three dora.

00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:37.990
That's a dealer baiman. 24,000.

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:40.490
<i>These girls...</i>

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:42.000
<i>surpass my expectations.</i>

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:44.670
Ron.

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:46.040
12,000.

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:48.290
<i>They're good.</i>

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:49.960
Ron.

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:51.670
12,000.

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:55.340
<i>This is national competition level.</i>

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:59.140
<i>These are the people who 
Nodoka went up against.</i>

00:09:02.360 --> 00:09:03.680
<i>All right...</i>

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:06.150
<i>We have to get stronger!</i>

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:08.110
<i>Get stronger!</i>

00:09:09.150 --> 00:09:10.070
<i>Get stronger...</i>

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:12.070
<i>Get stronger...</i>

00:09:13.030 --> 00:09:14.090
<i>Get stronger...</i>

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:21.820
Thanks for driving us home.

00:09:23.170 --> 00:09:25.700
Sorry we couldn't play you for very long.

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:27.190
Yumi-chin and Mippo

00:09:27.190 --> 00:09:28.910
have their game with Kiyosumi tomorrow,

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:31.140
so they insisted on going to bed early.

00:09:31.140 --> 00:09:32.320
This was more than enough.

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:34.010
Um... Kanbara-san?

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:34.760
Yeah?

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:37.940
Um, when you meet 
Kiyosumi... could you...

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:41.160
You don't have to finish that sentence.

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:43.570
We kind of understand what's going on.

00:09:43.570 --> 00:09:45.350
Thank you.

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:48.210
I feel like we got a very 
valuable hint today.

00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:51.400
Yeah! Since none of us are 
competing in the individuals,

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:53.150
we're free to do practice matches with

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:55.000
the players who are only in 
the individual tournament!

00:09:55.640 --> 00:09:58.450
Akado-san style surprise 
practice matches!

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:01.960
But we only have one day 
until the semifinals.

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:03.880
I still want to do as much as we can.

00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:06.310
Some players must have 
already come out to Tokyo!

00:10:06.310 --> 00:10:08.040
We could also use the time when

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:09.360
we are traveling or waiting to study

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:10.880
Shindouji's and Shiraitodai's records!

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:11.840
Let's do it!

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:13.520
Yeah!

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:28.770
<b>We're all practicing today.
Please don't worry about us.
-Arata</b>

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:27.270
What are you doing for breakfast, Arata?

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:28.140
Huh?

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:33.400
I see.

00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:37.020
No risk, no gain, huh?

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:42.790
It's really coming down.

00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:46.960
Thanks for coming all the way out here.

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:47.750
Sangamaki (North Osaka)
2nd Year
Arakawa Kei

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:47.750
Are you okay?

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:50.070
Yes, thanks for having us.

00:10:50.070 --> 00:10:50.950
A nurse?

00:10:50.950 --> 00:10:51.790
She's a nurse.

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:53.620
We simply tried to get in touch

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:55.690
with everyone we could,

00:10:55.690 --> 00:10:57.720
but you're the only one
 who got back to us.

00:10:57.720 --> 00:10:59.840
I guess that's to be expected, 
since we're just kids.

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:01.200
No problem.

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:03.550
We're happy to get the practice, too.

00:11:04.460 --> 00:11:05.890
"We"?

00:11:06.340 --> 00:11:07.970
I called a few people.

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:09.530
Come on in.

00:11:13.170 --> 00:11:14.650
I'll introduce you.

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:18.610
Kyuushuu Sekizan
(Kagoshima)
3rd Year
Fuijwara Rise

00:11:14.990 --> 00:11:16.990
From Kyuushuu Sekizan High School,

00:11:16.990 --> 00:11:18.650
this is Fujiwara Rise-san.

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:20.820
Moko-chan became the 
Toukai King just five months

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:22.760
after she started playing mahjong.

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:26.620
Kakuouzan (West Aichi)
1st Year
Tsuiki Moko

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:26.660
She's not playing in the team or 
individual tournaments at nationals.

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:30.160
This is her friend Nakiri-san, 
who's first in Shizuoka.

00:11:26.970 --> 00:11:30.140
Koudo Academy (Shizuoka)
2nd Year
Nakiri Ranko

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:34.150
Suwada (Chiba)
3rd year
Shimozaki Ito

00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:34.170
Suwada High School's 
Shimozaki-san is Chiba's MVP.

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:37.670
We'll be playing you guys.

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:39.730
This is great!

00:11:39.730 --> 00:11:41.930
We're looking forward to it!

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:43.700
Just leave it to us!

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:46.980
The third game will be a

00:11:46.980 --> 00:11:48.950
major attraction as Eisui 
Girls' High School will

00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:50.470
be facing Himematsu High School!

00:11:50.470 --> 00:11:53.160
Eisui's first player will be Jindai Komaki,

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:55.590
who was hugely successful in last year's

00:11:55.590 --> 00:11:57.320
team tournament!

00:11:57.800 --> 00:12:00.340
Iwate Prefecture's representative 
is Miyamori Girls' High School.

00:12:00.340 --> 00:12:03.180
They bested Makaku High School even 
though they had to face Mekaru,

00:12:03.180 --> 00:12:06.200
who placed 6th in the individuals last 
year, and moved on to round two!

00:12:06.530 --> 00:12:09.150
Their first player is Kosegawa Shiromi!

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:12.640
Placing 5th in the Spring Tournament 
and representing South Osaka

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:13.960
is Himematsu High School!

00:12:14.340 --> 00:12:15.920
Ueshige Suzu!

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:17.600
Last year she was the fourth player,

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:19.520
but this year she'll be the first player!

00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:21.430
Representing Nagano Prefecture,

00:12:21.430 --> 00:12:23.210
<i>we have Kiyosumi High School!</i>

00:12:23.210 --> 00:12:26.020
<i>They broke the banks of the other schools 
in the first round third players' match</i>

00:12:26.020 --> 00:12:27.780
<i>and advanced to round two!</i>

00:12:27.780 --> 00:12:30.550
<i>Their first player is Kataoka Yuuki!</i>

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:34.060
<i>Now, the first players' match 
is about to begin!</i>

00:12:48.750 --> 00:12:50.370
Thank you very much!

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:53.370
You're welcome. 
We had a lot of fun, too.

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:55.730
We'll be cheering for you 
in the team tournament,

00:12:55.730 --> 00:12:56.920
so do your best!

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:57.880
We will!

00:12:57.880 --> 00:13:00.090
Bye!

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:05.400
Fierce Mahjong Battle
National Competition
Mahjong Players...

00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:06.660
Fierce Mahjong Battle
68th Results
...Academy (Kagoshima)

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:08.320
Fierce Mahjong Battle
68th results

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:10.010
Fierce Mahjong Battle
The schools advancing to the semifinals decided...

00:13:25.630 --> 00:13:27.680
We're home!

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:31.200
I guess after a few nights, 
it starts feeling like home.

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:32.410
Yeah, huh?

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:34.310
That was pretty great though.

00:13:34.310 --> 00:13:34.870
Yeah.

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:37.860
At first, it was like we couldn't 
do anything against them,

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:40.210
but then I felt like 
I slowly got used to it.

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:42.260
We put up a good fight.

00:13:42.260 --> 00:13:43.440
That reminds me.

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:44.170
Huh?

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:46.880
I wonder if Nodoka won her game today.

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:51.640
I wonder.

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:52.630
I think...

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:55.520
it's better if we don't know.

00:13:56.460 --> 00:13:57.560
Yeah.

00:13:57.560 --> 00:13:59.970
Our motivation might decrease

00:13:59.970 --> 00:14:03.710
if we heard that Nodoka lost, right?

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:07.380
I guess so.

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:09.540
Good night, Arata-chan.

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:10.980
Good night.

00:14:10.980 --> 00:14:12.060
Good night.

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:23.460
Welcome back.

00:14:26.750 --> 00:14:28.050
I'm back.

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:33.640
You're not going to ask where we went?

00:14:33.990 --> 00:14:37.350
Naw, I trust you guys.

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:41.520
<i>She's basically given up on us!</i>

00:15:02.720 --> 00:15:06.090
I'm going to have to get more 
shampoo at the front desk.

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:07.650
Or maybe I should just buy my own.

00:15:07.650 --> 00:15:10.310
We're going to win that game tomorrow.

00:15:10.310 --> 00:15:11.680
Shizu?

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:14.080
Let's go to the drugstore later.

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:24.030
That's...

00:15:25.170 --> 00:15:27.050
Sorry, I'm going out for a sec!

00:15:28.110 --> 00:15:29.550
Oh well.

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:45.060
Kumakura-san!

00:15:50.780 --> 00:15:52.720
Can I help you?

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:54.150
Are you...

00:15:56.880 --> 00:15:59.480
Are you taking Akado-san with you again?

00:16:00.570 --> 00:16:02.700
Oh, you're...

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:05.670
I know going pro would be 
a great thing for her...

00:16:06.420 --> 00:16:08.790
but having that happen again would

00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:10.340
just be too hard on us...

00:16:10.340 --> 00:16:12.030
Oh, that.

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:13.990
She turned my offer down.

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:19.860
She said it would feel like she's only going 
pro because of her students' efforts.

00:16:19.860 --> 00:16:22.270
She said she'll stay 
with you until the end.

00:16:22.270 --> 00:16:24.880
After that, then she'll think
 about her professional career.

00:16:24.880 --> 00:16:26.790
Is that really true?!

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:29.870
I'm serious. Totally serious.

00:16:39.090 --> 00:16:40.680
Good luck.

00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:51.360
Ako!

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:52.490
Yeah?

00:16:54.820 --> 00:16:57.160
Don't scare me like that!

00:16:57.160 --> 00:16:58.480
What is it?

00:16:58.480 --> 00:16:59.520
Get everyone over here.

00:16:59.520 --> 00:17:01.500
Keep it a secret from Akado-san.

00:17:01.970 --> 00:17:03.370
Everyone?

00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:29.360
So Harue turned down the offer to go pro.

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:32.320
I'm sure she didn't do it 
just for us, but still.

00:17:40.650 --> 00:17:41.710
Darn it!

00:17:42.060 --> 00:17:43.670
Let's do our best in the semifinals!

00:17:43.670 --> 00:17:46.030
Senriyama is strong, 
Shiraitodai is strong!

00:17:46.030 --> 00:17:47.570
We know that!

00:17:48.170 --> 00:17:50.840
But we're stronger than we were this morning,

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:52.800
stronger than we've ever been before!

00:17:56.690 --> 00:17:58.800
Making it to the Top 4 would 
be a prefecture first.

00:18:01.070 --> 00:18:03.370
That's where Haru-chan wanted to go.

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:07.110
We're almost there.

00:18:13.620 --> 00:18:15.320
We will get there.

00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:19.070
With our own power!

00:18:24.680 --> 00:18:26.200
To the finals!

00:18:31.220 --> 00:18:33.330
Ryuuka, is something wrong?

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:40.770
Don't worry about me, Toki.

00:18:40.770 --> 00:18:42.480
We've got another early day tomorrow,

00:18:42.480 --> 00:18:44.000
so you should go to sleep.

00:18:47.300 --> 00:18:48.550
Good night.

00:18:49.790 --> 00:18:52.140
Good night, Toki.

00:18:55.680 --> 00:18:57.980
It's finally time!

00:18:57.980 --> 00:19:01.740
The seventh day of the Inter-high 
Tournament, the A Block semifinals!

00:19:01.740 --> 00:19:04.700
The fight to decide who'll 
be in the Top 4...

00:19:05.780 --> 00:19:07.190
is about to start!

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:08.540
Commentary, Announcer
Fukuyo Kouko

00:19:07.970 --> 00:19:09.540
Why are you making those 
strange gestures?

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:11.580
The mic is going to 
pick up weird noises.

00:19:09.560 --> 00:19:11.580
Analyst / Pro Player
Kokaji Sukoya

00:19:13.480 --> 00:19:15.560
Shall we just introduce 
the participants?

00:19:15.560 --> 00:19:17.370
I guess you have to.

00:19:17.370 --> 00:19:18.880
Then let's go!

00:19:20.950 --> 00:19:23.730
Representing Nara Prefecture, 
we've got the Achiga Girls' Academy

00:19:23.730 --> 00:19:25.870
playing in the nationals for 
the first time in ten years.

00:19:25.870 --> 00:19:30.140
Just like the first time, they 
have made it to the semifinals!

00:19:30.810 --> 00:19:33.400
Representing Fukuoka Prefecture 
is Shindouji Girls' High School.

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:35.210
The strongest school in North Kyuushuu

00:19:35.210 --> 00:19:36.850
returns again this year!

00:19:36.850 --> 00:19:39.330
Representing North Osaka is Senriyama Girls'.

00:19:39.330 --> 00:19:41.430
They placed fourth in last year's 
national championships,

00:19:41.430 --> 00:19:43.020
but have moved up in rank to second

00:19:43.020 --> 00:19:44.770
after the spring tournament results.

00:19:45.580 --> 00:19:49.200
And finally, we have Shiraitodai High School.

00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:50.800
As everybody knows, they are the

00:19:50.800 --> 00:19:52.850
reigning champions for the last two years!

00:19:52.850 --> 00:19:54.890
Some are calling them the strongest team

00:19:54.890 --> 00:19:56.540
in the national championships' history.

00:19:57.170 --> 00:19:59.810
Does that mean they're 
stronger than your team

00:19:59.810 --> 00:20:01.430
from twenty years ago?

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:05.350
I... well... I couldn't say.

00:20:06.190 --> 00:20:08.940
<i>That wasn't twenty years ago;
 it was ten years ago!</i>

00:20:08.940 --> 00:20:10.560
<i>Oh, really?</i>

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:13.230
<i>I could've sworn you were around forty.</i>

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:15.100
<i>I'm around thirty!</i>

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:16.400
I wish we could do the semifinals, too.

00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:18.840
Isn't it better that we're off?

00:20:18.840 --> 00:20:20.150
You think so?

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:21.890
<i>...making me imagine...</i>

00:20:21.890 --> 00:20:23.310
<i>But life's all about...</i>

00:20:23.310 --> 00:20:25.520
This new announcer is simply terrible.

00:20:25.520 --> 00:20:28.140
Is that some jealousy I sense?

00:20:29.000 --> 00:20:30.510
<i>What are you talking about?</i>

00:20:30.510 --> 00:20:35.310
<i>Well, fact is that the schools 
ranked 1st and 2nd are here,</i>

00:20:35.310 --> 00:20:38.020
<i>and I have high hopes 
for the other schools,</i>

00:20:38.020 --> 00:20:40.170
<i>so I think this is quite a great match-up.</i>

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:42.850
<i>In a moment, it's the first players' 
match. Our viewers should</i>

00:20:42.850 --> 00:20:45.340
<i>to the bathroom or get their food now.</i>

00:20:51.970 --> 00:20:53.890
Achiga Girls' (Nara)
2nd year - First Player
Matsumi Kuro

00:20:52.230 --> 00:20:53.890
Here I go.

00:20:53.890 --> 00:20:55.650
Go get 'em, Kuro!

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:57.360
Go, Kuro-san!

00:20:58.670 --> 00:21:01.360
Stay calm and play like you always do.

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:03.360
Fight, Kuro-chan.

00:21:04.260 --> 00:21:06.070
I got this, guys!

00:21:21.440 --> 00:21:25.420
Senriyama Girls' (North Osaka)
3rd Year - First Player
Onjouji Toki

00:21:43.730 --> 00:21:46.070
<i>That's the best high school player.</i>

00:21:46.300 --> 00:21:50.030
Shiraitodai High (West Tokyo)
3rd Year - First Player
Miyanaga Teru

00:21:47.800 --> 00:21:49.320
Miyanaga Teru!

00:21:51.460 --> 00:21:53.450
You're all here!

00:21:53.900 --> 00:21:55.510
That's super.

00:21:59.160 --> 00:22:01.980
After all, the best player 
always appears last!

00:21:59.730 --> 00:22:02.710
Shindouji Girls'  (Fukuoka)
2nd Year - First Player
Hanada Kirame

00:22:03.060 --> 00:22:06.720
Miyanaga-san really kicked 
my butt in the second round,

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:09.720
but I'm not losing today!

00:22:10.070 --> 00:22:11.760
Places have been decided and

00:22:11.760 --> 00:22:15.230
all four players have 
taken up their positions.

00:22:17.860 --> 00:22:19.120
<i>Toki...</i>

00:22:19.700 --> 00:22:21.400
<i>The match is about to begin!</i>

00:22:33.550 --> 00:22:36.620
<i>This is the first game of the 
National Competition's semifinals!</i>

00:22:37.550 --> 00:22:38.920
<i>Kuro-san!</i>

00:22:42.340 --> 00:22:43.770
Start!

00:24:04.940 --> 00:24:19.930
<b>Best</b>

00:24:07.280 --> 00:24:09.820
Hey, watch out. 
 What are you doing, Shizu?

00:24:09.820 --> 00:24:12.760
Hold the arms in close and 
explode out from inside!

00:24:12.760 --> 00:24:13.930
Shizu?

00:24:13.930 --> 00:24:17.470
Twist the body back and 
fly into a spinning jump!

00:24:17.470 --> 00:24:19.190
You have too much energy.

00:24:19.930 --> 00:25:00.000
<i>Please 
tune in again!</i>
